{
  "name": "VaNi GTM - Render Page",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "VaNi GTM — headless page render\n\nPOST /vani-render-page\nbody: { \"url\": \"https://…\" }\nheader: x-vani-secret  (validated by the webhook's Header Auth\ncredential — NO env vars, NO enterprise features)\n\nReturns { success, url, chars, html }.\nCalled by the VaNiGTM ingestion agent ONLY when a site's\nstatic HTML is too thin (JS-rendered SPA).\n\nSETUP (once):\n1. Install community node: Settings → Community Nodes →\n   n8n-nodes-puppeteer  (BEFORE importing this workflow)\n2. Create credential: Credentials → New → Header Auth →\n   Name: 'VaNi Render Secret', Header Name: x-vani-secret,\n   Header Value: <long random string>\n3. Open the Webhook node and select that credential.\n4. Activate this workflow.\nBackend needs: N8N_RENDER_URL, N8N_RENDER_SECRET (same value),\nN8N_ENV=live for /webhook (else /webhook-test is used).",
        "height": 560,
        "width": 420,
        "color": 5
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [-2464, -16],
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "id": "a1b2c3d4-0001-4000-8000-000000000001",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Render Page"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "vani-render-page",
        "authentication": "headerAuth",
        "responseMode": "responseNode",
        "options": {}
      },
      "name": "Render Page Webhook",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
      "position": [-1980, 200],
      "id": "a1b2c3d4-0002-4000-8000-000000000002",
      "webhookId": "vani-render-page-001",
      "credentials": {
        "httpHeaderAuth": {
          "name": "VaNi Render Secret"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "boolean": [
            {
              "value1": "={{ $json.body.url !== undefined && $json.body.url.startsWith('http') }}",
              "value2": true
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "name": "Validate Render Input",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [-1772, 200],
      "id": "a1b2c3d4-0003-4000-8000-000000000003"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "keepOnlySet": true,
        "values": {
          "string": [
            { "name": "status", "value": "error" },
            { "name": "errorCode", "value": "INVALID_INPUT_OR_AUTH" },
            { "name": "message", "value": "Missing or invalid url" },
            { "name": "suggestion", "value": "Send { \"url\": \"https://…\" } in the request body" }
          ],
          "boolean": [
            { "name": "success", "value": false },
            { "name": "recoverable", "value": false }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "name": "Invalid Render Input",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [-1564, 360],
      "id": "a1b2c3d4-0004-4000-8000-000000000004"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "keepOnlySet": true,
        "values": {
          "string": [
            { "name": "url", "value": "={{ $json.body.url }}" }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "name": "Prepare Render Data",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [-1564, 120],
      "id": "a1b2c3d4-0005-4000-8000-000000000005"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "getPageContent",
        "url": "={{ $json.url }}",
        "options": {
          "waitUntil": "networkidle2",
          "timeout": 45000
        }
      },
      "name": "Render Page (Puppeteer)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-puppeteer.puppeteer",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [-1356, 120],
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "maxTries": 2,
      "waitBetweenTries": 2000,
      "id": "a1b2c3d4-0006-4000-8000-000000000006",
      "continueOnFail": true
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Normalize across n8n-nodes-puppeteer versions: HTML may land in\n// body / data / html. Empty or errored → structured error (no silent ok).\nconst item = $input.first().json;\nconst url = $('Prepare Render Data').first().json.url;\n\nif (item.error !== undefined) {\n  return {\n    success: false,\n    status: 'error',\n    errorCode: 'RENDER_FAILED',\n    message: 'Headless render failed',\n    details: String(item.error?.message || item.error).slice(0, 300),\n    url,\n    recoverable: true\n  };\n}\n\nconst html = item.body || item.data || item.html || '';\nif (typeof html !== 'string' || html.length < 100) {\n  return {\n    success: false,\n    status: 'error',\n    errorCode: 'RENDER_EMPTY',\n    message: 'Renderer returned no HTML',\n    details: `got ${typeof html === 'string' ? html.length : typeof html} — page may have blocked the browser`,\n    url,\n    recoverable: true\n  };\n}\n\nreturn {\n  success: true,\n  url,\n  chars: html.length,\n  html\n};"
      },
      "name": "Format Render Result",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [-1148, 120],
      "id": "a1b2c3d4-0007-4000-8000-000000000007"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "boolean": [
            {
              "value1": "={{ $json.success === true }}",
              "value2": true
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "name": "Render OK?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [-940, 120],
      "id": "a1b2c3d4-0008-4000-8000-000000000008"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "respondWith": "json",
        "responseBody": "={{ $json }}",
        "options": { "responseCode": 200 }
      },
      "name": "Respond Render Success",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.respondToWebhook",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [-732, 0],
      "id": "a1b2c3d4-0009-4000-8000-000000000009"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "name": "Merge Render Errors",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.merge",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [-940, 360],
      "id": "a1b2c3d4-0010-4000-8000-000000000010"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "respondWith": "json",
